#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128989 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129170 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec44686a-601b-52b3-81df-e57e6708fb93" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Multiplicative Property"}] :question/id #uuid "53185b25-c690-500a-9a82-c18b37668e27" :question/math-academy-id "e-6106" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{R} xy\\ \\!e^{x+y}\\ \\textrm d A$ over the rectangle $R= [0,1] \\times [1,2].$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\iint\\limits_{R}  xy\\  e^{x+y}\\: \\textrm d A &= \\iint\\limits_{R} \\Big( x\\ \\! e^x \\Big)\\Big( y\\ \\! e^{y} \\Big) \\textrm d A\\[5pt]\n&= \\left(\\int_0^1x\\  e^{x}  \\ \\textrm d x\\right)\\left( \\int_1^2 y \\ \\!e^{y} \\ \\textrm d y\\right)\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &= \\Big[x\\ \\!e^x-e^x\\Big]_0^1 \\cdot  \\Big[y\\ \\!e^y-e^y\\Big]_1^2\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &=  \\Big(e^1-e^1 - \\left(0-e^0\\right)\\Big) \\cdot \\Big(2e^2-e^2 - \\left(e^1-e^1\\right) \\Big)\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &= 1\\cdot e^2\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &= e^2\n}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128990 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "307bccb6-036f-51bb-99ce-327aad8dfdbe" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral When the Integrand Contains Only One Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "a5567cb9-1c16-56a6-b0e8-759edf693a41" :question/math-academy-id "e-6107" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{R} \\left(x^2-y^2 +3\\right)  \\textrm d A,$  where $R= [-1,3] \\times [2, 4].$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+3)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{R}3\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's evaluate each of the three integrals.\n\n- The function under the first integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(4-2){\\int }_{-1}^{3}{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{-1}^{3} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{27}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{56}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function under the second integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(3-(-1)){\\int }_{2}^{4}{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{2}^{4}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{4}^{3}-\\frac{4}{3}{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{224}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function under the third integral is a constant, so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}3\\,\\text{d}A=3\\,\\text{Area}(R)=3\\cdot (2\\cdot 4)=24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}A=\\frac{56}{3}-\\frac{224}{3}+24=-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128991 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8059a197-e9fb-5306-8eed-62c0cea88f33" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Additivity Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/id #uuid "0cb8fa8a-5be1-5f53-bfde-5acf325f6332" :question/math-academy-id "e-6108" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{R}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm d A$, where\n\n![](images/60/606ce428283013cc4e3e5969b634d5536a61f8512c98a627a582816c7de02338.svg)\nand  $R$ is the domain of $f.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we have $R = R_1 \\cup R_2,$ where $R_1= (0,2) \\times (-1,0)$ and $R_2= (0,2) \\times (0,1).$ So, we can write\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\iint\\limits_{R}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm d A &= \\iint\\limits_{R_1} 2 \\ \\textrm d A + \\iint\\limits_{R_2}    \\dfrac{1}{xy+x+y+1} \\ \\textrm d A\\[5pt]\n&= 2\\iint\\limits_{R_1} \\textrm d A\n+ \\iint\\limits_{R_2}  \\dfrac{1}{(x+1)(y+1)} \\ \\textrm d A\\[5pt]\n&= 2(2-0)(0-(-1)) + \\Bigg( \\int_0^2 \\dfrac{1}{x+1} \\ \\textrm d x \\Bigg) \\Bigg( \\int_0^1 \\dfrac{1}{y+1}\\ \\textrm d y \\Bigg) \\[5pt]\n&= 4 + \\Big[\\ln(x+1)\\Big]_0^2  \\cdot \\Big[\\ln(y+1)\\Big]_0^1\\[5pt] \n&= 4+ \\ln 3\\ln 2.\n}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129007 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129188 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8505beff-75b8-57bf-9312-e0fcf32f44fd" :knowledge-point/title "Using Additivity of Double Integrals"}] :question/id #uuid "1c227b12-d40b-53a8-b568-b7bd380acbee" :question/math-academy-id "e-7023" :question/problem "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{C}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A = 8,\n\\qquad\n\\iint\\limits_{D}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A = -5,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{C \\cup D}  3f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}3f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =3{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =3(8+(-5)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129170 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec44686a-601b-52b3-81df-e57e6708fb93" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Multiplicative Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a378edd-d1db-54be-8ae5-9e0226579fe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263099} {:answer/id #uuid "59f33436-7f66-5478-8678-a904b0cee1cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263774} {:answer/id #uuid "9035a538-ae3d-523c-a179-a40d9c624887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264237} {:answer/id #uuid "a93da0d5-f65a-551b-8cbf-6896d7bc2a0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264446} {:answer/id #uuid "f5763788-64a2-5349-a547-102278dfe27d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5763788-64a2-5349-a547-102278dfe27d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265149} :answer-field/id #uuid "50480348-e538-5444-bff1-bc0785876c6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "78952ad2-30a2-59fb-b1fc-a12708c43533" :question/math-academy-id "q-129937" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[0,\\pi ]\\times [0,2].$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(\\frac{1}{4+{y}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi }\\cdot [\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{2})]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-(-1-1)\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{8}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380859 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129170 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec44686a-601b-52b3-81df-e57e6708fb93" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Multiplicative Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67efca7f-46bf-526b-bf7c-9f183d920665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380861} {:answer/id #uuid "d1de4ab0-12a4-59ba-8566-42bcdbebcac3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380862} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d9b309-5a55-5235-872f-d5104ba02de6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380863} {:answer/id #uuid "78355ea5-cab7-5cce-b31c-f99ccd2eb4b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380864} {:answer/id #uuid "4504705a-4b07-5eef-b515-b9593cf1b9ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4504705a-4b07-5eef-b515-b9593cf1b9ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380865} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a844585-2a8a-5020-bb6d-497af9fa7a7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380860}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4e6ad635-fec2-5b1b-906a-f0e5dc3a4875" :question/math-academy-id "q-129940" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{xy}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[1,e]\\times [e,{e}^{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{xy}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{x})\\text{ }(\\frac{1}{y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{e}\\cdot [\\operatorname{ln}⁡y]_{e}^{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡e) \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445488 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "307bccb6-036f-51bb-99ce-327aad8dfdbe" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral When the Integrand Contains Only One Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f7f1c17-e012-579b-b10d-42979ace1885" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445447} {:answer/id #uuid "22bea2a1-3640-54bb-b37a-5be01206ddd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445448} {:answer/id #uuid "4a778fe7-65d5-579b-bbd4-ac73193b8148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445457} {:answer/id #uuid "842cd6fa-cc72-5447-a959-3164db0ba831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445464} {:answer/id #uuid "948fb597-3610-520a-bb28-3ef09776ffb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22bea2a1-3640-54bb-b37a-5be01206ddd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445448} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9a8646d-83af-52fd-a349-459e6460b606" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4bacfe6-30e7-5d9e-a1c2-df77375c3f7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-129955" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{6+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[0,3]\\times [1,2].$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{6+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{6}{{y}^{2}}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{R}\\frac{6}{{y}^{2}}\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{R}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{6}{{y}^{2}}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(3-0){\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{6}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-\\frac{6}{y}{|}_{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =-18(\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & =(2-1){\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}-0 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{6+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A=9+9=18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445485 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129188 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8505beff-75b8-57bf-9312-e0fcf32f44fd" :knowledge-point/title "Using Additivity of Double Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24d7484c-3ae5-5063-8b35-977a513d4bd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445450} {:answer/id #uuid "7724f8f2-18ad-546b-9e22-590fc275f5e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445459} {:answer/id #uuid "af701f69-f74a-509d-94be-0d22341fdc2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445470} {:answer/id #uuid "c4559e50-3f4e-5b00-af09-75d0e5472202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445473} {:answer/id #uuid "cbdb1160-1c9e-5a17-94d0-e98a44eb4815" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbdb1160-1c9e-5a17-94d0-e98a44eb4815" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445474} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8602de3-643b-512d-8235-9d9217ba8f38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445481}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9794b451-1881-5349-8cf7-09e2d5dcd1d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-130019" :question/problem "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=-3,\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=11,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n{∬}_{C\\cup D}\\frac{1}{4}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}\\frac{1}{4}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =\\frac{1}{4}{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(-3+11) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380887 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129188 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8505beff-75b8-57bf-9312-e0fcf32f44fd" :knowledge-point/title "Using Additivity of Double Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7ca0fab-075f-5734-9404-a0116b2b5481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S\\cup U}(\\sqrt{xy}+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380889} {:answer/id #uuid "65875c7d-3c02-56d4-92cd-11bf2395175e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380890} {:answer/id #uuid "e0651f3a-2e5d-5164-a133-6b270af1e639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380891} {:answer/id #uuid "2dd6a7f4-7b19-555f-b262-2eb0eacf2344" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S\\cup U}\\sqrt{xy}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380892} {:answer/id #uuid "edf299a8-ceef-5a1c-956d-ec8ef1c226fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65875c7d-3c02-56d4-92cd-11bf2395175e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380890} :answer-field/id #uuid "75a5c930-1ca9-58b5-8264-1a5886ebc360" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8a2d9ca-ceb2-572b-acd2-d44a9e37ec8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130022" :question/problem "![](images/aa/aae6528f576b58fb5cea5238a921074d2176f9e9c9e6fc0ba3e98bc2f647e133.png)\n\nConsider the region $R$ shown above. Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{xy}, & (x,y)\\in S, \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in T, \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain $R$ can be represented as a union of three sub-domains, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =S\\cup T\\cup U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{S}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}0\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380901 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129188 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8505beff-75b8-57bf-9312-e0fcf32f44fd" :knowledge-point/title "Using Additivity of Double Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7db9ae6-022f-576a-8519-7658f21f3c1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380903} {:answer/id #uuid "02402e02-1c0d-5866-945c-89ed5fcb73d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380904} {:answer/id #uuid "cf442e6d-ef62-56e6-b29f-779c57161862" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380905} {:answer/id #uuid "cf6d7190-82e1-5ea8-9682-d27614c71d44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380906} {:answer/id #uuid "1a6d80d9-2c44-5055-a96b-4b1146cdd341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02402e02-1c0d-5866-945c-89ed5fcb73d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380904} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e73b362-62bb-5798-aa2e-4d6f0042c275" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380902}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09109a55-6e5b-5bb8-a3bc-8b73ba148056" :question/math-academy-id "q-130025" :question/problem "![](images/dd/ddc6c02aff017b31dd24ba6d47a3527aa46a2a5130cffc7094122545babd7656.png)\n\nConsider the region $R$ shown above. Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x, & (x,y)\\in S, \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in T, \\\\ {e}^{x+y}, & (x,y)\\in U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain $R$ can be represented as a union of three sub-domains, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =S\\cup T\\cup U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{S}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}0\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265804 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8059a197-e9fb-5306-8eed-62c0cea88f33" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Additivity Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e35ef35-ff48-5e0e-b45c-16d9c9d6eb80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,2)}\\frac{y+1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (2,4)}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263953} {:answer/id #uuid "c3308c3c-38ac-5e02-8bb3-09f266686a29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,4)}(\\frac{y+1}{1+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264701} {:answer/id #uuid "eb6905fa-dfd2-5209-96b6-0a3467859dae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,2)}\\frac{y+1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(2,4)\\times (2,4)}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265055} {:answer/id #uuid "ec02c144-31a5-5879-a3d0-81ee338bad48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,4)}\\frac{{x}^{2}(y+1)}{{y}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265065} {:answer/id #uuid "f38d6811-6741-50d2-bbf2-973c0069b778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,2)}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (2,4)}\\frac{y+1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e35ef35-ff48-5e0e-b45c-16d9c9d6eb80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,2)}\\frac{y+1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (2,4)}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263953} :answer-field/id #uuid "88b62c52-192d-530f-aa19-1533d59dee25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4097ab0e-1da6-536a-8ecd-ac95516f4e76" :question/math-academy-id "q-130038" :question/problem "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y+1}{1+{x}^{2}},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<2,\\,1<y<2, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<2,\\,2<y<4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,4)}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the rectangle $R$ can be represented as a union of two smaller rectangles, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =(1,2)\\times ((1,2)\\cup (2,4)) \\\\  & =((1,2)\\times (1,2))\\cup ((1,2)\\times (2,4)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,2)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (2,4)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,2)}\\frac{y+1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (2,4)}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265807 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8059a197-e9fb-5306-8eed-62c0cea88f33" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Additivity Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e56985f-4995-5832-bc47-741b2c1c4d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263389} {:answer/id #uuid "2f850b1b-56d0-59fe-a9ae-66a9e18b21ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263400} {:answer/id #uuid "368fce54-dfc9-5cf7-bfed-6e49c5c536c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263482} {:answer/id #uuid "5242a3d0-9686-5c9e-8bd4-51f9d91b6046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263708} {:answer/id #uuid "a0e848e1-2f47-546b-a791-34c55dd61aef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5242a3d0-9686-5c9e-8bd4-51f9d91b6046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263708} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b2c7ebf-14a9-54f0-9253-98e711bf656a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a400e754-c19b-557c-be08-7c8b69cf6b10" :question/math-academy-id "q-130042" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$, where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{2},\\, & \\text{if}\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<2, \\\\ 2x,\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<1,\\,0<y<2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  $R$ is the domain of $f.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we have $R={R}_{1}\\cup {R}_{2}$, where ${R}_{1}=(-2,0)\\times (0,2)$ and ${R}_{2}=(0,1)\\times (0,2).$ So, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A= & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}2x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}(x)({y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}2x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{-2}^{0}x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)+(2-0){\\int }_{0}^{1}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{-2}^{0}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2}+2[{x}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot \\frac{8}{3}+2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265808 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8059a197-e9fb-5306-8eed-62c0cea88f33" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Additivity Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fabc10d-9ae1-5e94-853a-462fb1aa00c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263139} {:answer/id #uuid "36198322-ecf6-5863-a4a5-ad9f61a2c642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{2}+2e-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263479} {:answer/id #uuid "4ec19f8f-0bbe-587e-b732-392919b19297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}-e+14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263684} {:answer/id #uuid "5e93e174-ae19-5d17-a706-ca4ec3c6bb1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{2}+2e-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263817} {:answer/id #uuid "a416981c-bb03-5879-bcbc-2040c346ee71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{2}-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e93e174-ae19-5d17-a706-ca4ec3c6bb1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{2}+2e-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263817} :answer-field/id #uuid "49302468-b7d7-52f5-907e-c6fdfd044bfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a87d3263-74f6-5090-88d6-56cb978e87ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-130044" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$, where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y{e}^{x+1},\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<1,\\,-2<y<0, \\\\ 3y\\sqrt{x},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<4,\\,-2<y<0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  $R$ is the domain of $f.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we have $R={R}_{1}\\cup {R}_{2}$, where ${R}_{1}=(0,1)\\times (-2,0)$ and ${R}_{2}=(1,4)\\times (-2,0).$ So, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A= & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}y{e}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}3y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}({e}^{x+1})(y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}(\\sqrt{x})(3y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{-2}^{0}y\\,\\text{d}y)+({\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{-2}^{0}3y\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[{e}^{x+1}]_{0}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{-2}^{0}+{[\\frac{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3}]}_{1}^{4}\\cdot {[\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =({e}^{2}-e)\\cdot (0-2)+(\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{2}{3})\\cdot (0-6) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2}+2e-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129846 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129170 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec44686a-601b-52b3-81df-e57e6708fb93" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Multiplicative Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0737a4d6-7922-501a-85e2-cdcacd965620" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{4}y\\sqrt{y}\\,\\text{d}y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445442} {:answer/id #uuid "18dd8f5f-c7eb-5382-bc1d-0f430199a813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\sqrt{y}\\,\\text{d}y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445445} {:answer/id #uuid "1afa2a07-066e-5cde-b4a1-d851ce37e441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({\\int }_{1}^{4}y\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\text{d}y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445446} {:answer/id #uuid "3b3a5306-0d77-5431-97ec-aee41d4fd86f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{4}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445452} {:answer/id #uuid "9a0c2114-11bc-5668-ad0f-23cafddd72c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({\\int }_{1}^{4}y\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18dd8f5f-c7eb-5382-bc1d-0f430199a813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\sqrt{y}\\,\\text{d}y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445445} :answer-field/id #uuid "78d891bd-9431-5998-b4cc-257c16f65963" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7c6301d0-9292-5129-9703-537c7f2895a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-71933" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the value of the double integral ${∬}_{R}y\\sqrt{xy}\\text{ }\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[1,4]\\times [0,1]?$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}y\\sqrt{xy}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}y\\,{x}^{1/2}\\,{y}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{R}({x}^{1/2})\\text{ }({y}^{3/2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\sqrt{y}\\,\\text{d}y)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129848 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "307bccb6-036f-51bb-99ce-327aad8dfdbe" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral When the Integrand Contains Only One Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dc8e0ee-42d1-5e33-ab3e-d149ce209193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128574} {:answer/id #uuid "216a895e-32d8-5d87-938d-db65b2d1bddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19e-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419645} {:answer/id #uuid "4a5a35ab-9584-5250-9b05-bab514871947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19-20e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419646} {:answer/id #uuid "c482d14a-968e-5fba-92dc-75544ab448dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20-19e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419647} {:answer/id #uuid "c6534224-e681-59ea-874f-2267428a83f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16+20e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c482d14a-968e-5fba-92dc-75544ab448dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20-19e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419647} :answer-field/id #uuid "5432046c-908f-53bb-aa5e-d0f6af32c211" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a9bb5733-5b86-5301-9267-6ae190810785" :question/math-academy-id "q-71994" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{1-3x{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[1,e]\\times [2,3].$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1-3x{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{x}-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}3{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(3-2){\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|]_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}3{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(e-1){\\int }_{2}^{3}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =(e-1)[{y}^{3}]_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =(e-1)({3}^{3}-{2}^{3}) \\\\  & =19(e-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1-3x{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}A=1-19(e-1)=20-19e.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348401 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129170 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec44686a-601b-52b3-81df-e57e6708fb93" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Multiplicative Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45813fa4-fac0-5452-9255-9d2cc5a09b20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345956} {:answer/id #uuid "5837a18a-ae8a-5078-b71f-c3ebdbb5af5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346106} {:answer/id #uuid "92622851-e5da-5c25-8c6c-1a4734ebd54b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346632} {:answer/id #uuid "ac9f3b3e-4a16-5638-8f30-348e6dacf30a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346857} {:answer/id #uuid "acd4a2a8-18a1-55b8-81a7-2cf19b948e4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45813fa4-fac0-5452-9255-9d2cc5a09b20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345956} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b7b34a4-1322-5681-a0fb-3dfd4c852dbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "813cfc16-7a47-56e2-b9f6-16d7ae4bba08" :question/math-academy-id "q-80507" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[1,e]\\times [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{x})(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{e}\\cdot [\\operatorname{sin}⁡y]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445484 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129170 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec44686a-601b-52b3-81df-e57e6708fb93" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Multiplicative Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36c96f45-849b-5559-9bf5-b2baa5552f82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445451} {:answer/id #uuid "81d3eef9-452b-5246-977a-3d6437685e16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445463} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6ba610-9741-52ca-9ca3-ad5ada7c05b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445469} {:answer/id #uuid "b33e5d43-cfa1-503d-a04e-f819581e6ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445471} {:answer/id #uuid "ff4624ca-0d05-58ce-acd8-870bbeb876b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81d3eef9-452b-5246-977a-3d6437685e16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445463} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b4c1a25-c7e8-5e0a-820b-a6b872059bec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "68e39739-c077-5ff6-83ad-f603767a81a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-80510" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}{y}^{2}{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2}]\\times [0,3].$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}{y}^{2}{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}({csc}^{2}⁡x)({y}^{2})\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x]_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\\cdot (\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{0}^{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =(0+1)\\cdot (9-0) \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "307bccb6-036f-51bb-99ce-327aad8dfdbe" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral When the Integrand Contains Only One Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33574ba8-3a68-52a4-a29c-cefd3e428f26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345796} {:answer/id #uuid "88335118-c9d5-54e9-9421-6b4f5e015107" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346531} {:answer/id #uuid "8b64d300-35ac-5d4f-b0f0-df7f7ad345c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346558} {:answer/id #uuid "ab6239a6-a7ec-58f7-8e02-311f1bd7d30c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346845} {:answer/id #uuid "ff960c84-9159-57ba-a8e5-03395c0f4a78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab6239a6-a7ec-58f7-8e02-311f1bd7d30c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346845} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d0f1daa-3bd2-5289-b634-a2841e1fd2bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a3840370-2613-5223-99ab-f0ad1e415b85" :question/math-academy-id "q-80626" :question/problem "Calculate ${∬}_{R}(2+2x-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[0,3]\\times [0,2].$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(2+2x-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}2\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is a constant, so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}2\\,\\text{d}A=2\\,\\text{Area}(R)=2\\cdot (3\\cdot 2)=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}A & =(2-0){\\int }_{0}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot [{x}^{2}]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =2({3}^{2}-(0)^{2}) \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the third integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}2y\\,\\text{d}A & =(3-0){\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3\\cdot [{y}^{3}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =3({2}^{3}-{0}^{3}) \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(2+2x-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A=12+18-24=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382407 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "307bccb6-036f-51bb-99ce-327aad8dfdbe" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral When the Integrand Contains Only One Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8458ae4-fafc-5a98-ab45-1adea4f03cfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382409} {:answer/id #uuid "9addff4c-74aa-5855-b730-fe68fa5f33b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382410} {:answer/id #uuid "e32440d6-fac7-5caf-bfd7-7612653eb6a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382411} {:answer/id #uuid "8f95079d-845f-5ed2-b0b9-f6e1b9a61490" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382412} {:answer/id #uuid "e93d0ef7-1d27-53c3-becc-c9dfd0fe94fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9addff4c-74aa-5855-b730-fe68fa5f33b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382410} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc0d3863-9fe2-5bb6-8578-90c9d149b878" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "66d9f9e9-c9db-5bd9-aeae-e3f4c6b82bbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-80642" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{1+y{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[1,2]\\times [0,8].$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1+y{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{R}y\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A & =(8-0){\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}{|}_{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{8}-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}y\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(2-1){\\int }_{0}^{8}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{{8}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1+y{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A=3+32=35.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445483 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8059a197-e9fb-5306-8eed-62c0cea88f33" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Additivity Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b57a437-d5b0-5a5d-b1ff-35d38a6dde20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,1)\\times (0,1)}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A\\text{ }+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (0,1)}{e}^{(x-y)}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445443} {:answer/id #uuid "4420423b-4450-5202-b0cc-f36730793a82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,1)\\times (0,1)}{e}^{(x-y)}\\,\\text{d}A\\text{ }+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (0,1)}(x-y)\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445455} {:answer/id #uuid "6476986e-34b1-5256-b5dd-66cd4a918d16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,1)\\times (0,1)}{e}^{(x+y)}\\,\\text{d}A\\text{ }+{∬}_{(0,1)\\times (0,1)}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445458} {:answer/id #uuid "8af31339-6b09-525f-b717-5f12cc5c4fcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,1)\\times (0,1)}{e}^{(x-y)}\\,\\text{d}A\\text{ }+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (0,1)}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445465} {:answer/id #uuid "934ab2fb-0ff6-58be-abfc-b6ac610f4406" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,1)\\times (0,1)}{e}^{(x+y)}\\,\\text{d}A\\text{ }+{∬}_{(0,2)\\times (0,1)}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b57a437-d5b0-5a5d-b1ff-35d38a6dde20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,1)\\times (0,1)}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A\\text{ }+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (0,1)}{e}^{(x-y)}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445443} :answer-field/id #uuid "715fd868-4860-5d80-b1ca-fd540ecc3dd6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445479}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f7e7929-7b85-5acd-be84-f40a79eeb887" :question/math-academy-id "q-80662" :question/problem "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<1,\\,0<y<1, \\\\ {e}^{(x-y)},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<2,\\,0<y<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{(0,2)\\times (0,1)}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the rectangle $R$ can be represented as a union of two smaller rectangles, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =((0,1)\\cup (1,2))\\times (0,1) \\\\  & =((0,1)\\times (0,1))\\cup ((1,2)\\times (0,1)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{(0,1)\\times (0,1)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (0,1)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{(0,1)\\times (0,1)}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (0,1)}{e}^{(x-y)}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351275 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "307bccb6-036f-51bb-99ce-327aad8dfdbe" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral When the Integrand Contains Only One Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "634b37ae-308d-5435-a52f-c26d5dbb3de5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18-15e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349355} {:answer/id #uuid "88c60fb4-943d-5220-a08b-275dd68bbae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15e-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349688} {:answer/id #uuid "9cbd516c-5d24-5d14-9a48-94dcabde4994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12-15e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349843} {:answer/id #uuid "bb08d76a-f17e-5afb-83a6-3c276ee6efb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18e-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350107} {:answer/id #uuid "c92b28e8-5388-5912-966b-9e3d07de2e33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15-12e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "634b37ae-308d-5435-a52f-c26d5dbb3de5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18-15e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349355} :answer-field/id #uuid "869d9657-8796-582f-a842-5bede07c39d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af621e2e-fd54-5586-bdc4-d3d2f33437c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-81243" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{3-4y{x}^{3}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[1,2]\\times [1,e].$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{3-4y{x}^{3}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{3}{y}-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{R}\\frac{3}{y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}4{x}^{3}\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{3}{y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(2-1){\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{3}{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|]_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}4{x}^{3}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(e-1){\\int }_{1}^{2}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(e-1)[{x}^{4}]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(e-1)({2}^{4}-{1}^{4}) \\\\  & =15(e-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{3-4y{x}^{3}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A=3-15(e-1)=18-15e.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445487 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129188 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8505beff-75b8-57bf-9312-e0fcf32f44fd" :knowledge-point/title "Using Additivity of Double Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dd10fb2-a06b-597a-9fc7-9460e0a38b79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\text{ }\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445444} {:answer/id #uuid "239b5809-9ce8-5dea-8734-26328a32ffea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\text{ }\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445449} {:answer/id #uuid "4462f986-7acc-5f17-a7aa-2ecb6de29a48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{T}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\text{ }\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445456} {:answer/id #uuid "7943674e-8350-5027-ab62-6e0d1956e933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\text{ }\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445460} {:answer/id #uuid "c134de05-6a5a-5052-989b-8f259ce1ac90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\text{ }\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4462f986-7acc-5f17-a7aa-2ecb6de29a48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{T}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\text{ }\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445456} :answer-field/id #uuid "48a4b43a-bc8c-5a55-9d9f-8d40124bc6f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c07dad32-9851-5aba-9075-fbf7d573fb0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-81247" :question/problem "![](images/bc/bcc2eb6cd27450375016677390700675e9733c03dfd2c0100622e6f8c7d18e78.png)\n\nConsider the region $R$ shown above. Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & (x,y)\\in S, \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in T, \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain $D$ can be represented as a union of three sub-domains, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =S\\cup T\\cup U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{S}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}0\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{T}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129188 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8505beff-75b8-57bf-9312-e0fcf32f44fd" :knowledge-point/title "Using Additivity of Double Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab529760-3889-51a8-b4c8-66bfbf77c410" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{T}(\\sqrt[3]{x}y-\\sqrt[3]{y})\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382457} {:answer/id #uuid "2325dd1a-ce3d-54f1-afa1-cd4830f6be26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}\\sqrt[3]{x}\\text{ }\\text{d}A-{∬}_{T}y\\sqrt[3]{y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382458} {:answer/id #uuid "e9526d42-7973-5cd9-a423-f18f92adf041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}(\\sqrt[3]{x}y-\\sqrt[3]{y})\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382459} {:answer/id #uuid "a1c99a0e-5c23-54ec-aa7b-84c58c6240f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}(\\sqrt[3]{x}y-\\sqrt[3]{y})\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382460} {:answer/id #uuid "2b4d8952-e530-5523-a7fc-b0dd32bd0156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}\\sqrt[3]{x}y\\text{ }\\text{d}A-{∬}_{T}\\sqrt[3]{y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9526d42-7973-5cd9-a423-f18f92adf041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}(\\sqrt[3]{x}y-\\sqrt[3]{y})\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382459} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d9e42d1-446a-551f-9c15-70d2ade4d9dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6c01f4d5-f15d-5491-b498-84e3a762539b" :question/math-academy-id "q-81248" :question/problem "![](images/20/208f19ed915ad8db5f818636fe7b5d6f525487039195281346fc301a79638a6d.png)\n\nConsider the region $R$ shown above. Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{x}y-\\sqrt[3]{y}, & (x,y)\\in S, \\\\ 2x{y}^{3}, & (x,y)\\in T, \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain $R$ can be represented as a union of three sub-domains, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =S\\cup T\\cup U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{S}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}(\\sqrt[3]{x}y-\\sqrt[3]{y})\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}0\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}(\\sqrt[3]{x}y-\\sqrt[3]{y})\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8059a197-e9fb-5306-8eed-62c0cea88f33" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Additivity Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c07a49b-7df9-594b-b205-67f90501842d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (0,2)}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (0,2)}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445453} {:answer/id #uuid "421d54ba-8758-5066-8e3e-38909ec2e2da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(-1,0)\\times (0,2)}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,1)\\times (0,2)}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445454} {:answer/id #uuid "7adbe63b-2db0-59cf-9b4f-f2e0611fddb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (0,1)}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (1,2)}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445461} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0faed7-4a17-5ff4-8621-3575f43df76e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(-1,1)}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,1)}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445462} {:answer/id #uuid "f172a015-8a01-5667-8b61-667a981d09c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,1)}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(-1,1)}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7adbe63b-2db0-59cf-9b4f-f2e0611fddb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (0,1)}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (1,2)}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445461} :answer-field/id #uuid "c116b0e2-e431-5aed-b05a-a7ba568545f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b71bb968-9c3f-5d3e-ba1d-d7915e2cf55e" :question/math-academy-id "q-81251" :question/problem "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y},\\, & \\text{if}\\,-1<x<1,\\,0<y<1, \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y,\\, & \\text{if}\\,-1<x<1,\\,1<y<2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (0,2)}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the rectangle $R$ can be represented as a union of two smaller rectangles, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =(-1,1)\\times ((0,1)\\cup (1,2)) \\\\  & =((-1,1)\\times (0,1))\\cup ((-1,1)\\times (1,2)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (0,1)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (1,2)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (0,1)}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (1,2)}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
